# Board game architecture rules

This is a Godot 4 turn-based board game.

The game should be built as a headless rules engine first.

## Core principle

The UI is only a window into the game. The game itself is the state machine.

## Architecture rules

- Build the game as a headless rules engine first.
- The core game must be playable without UI, scenes, buttons, mouse input, sprites, animation, or rendering.
- Keep all core rules under `godot_game/core/` (or `res://core/` within the Godot project).
- Keep visual/debug UI under `godot_game/ui/`.
- Core code should be deterministic from a seed.
- The same seed plus the same legal actions must always produce the same result.
- Rules should mutate `GameState` only through explicit rule functions.
- Rule functions should return events describing what happened.
- The UI must only read state and events; it must not contain rules logic.
- Always add or update tests for any rule change.
- Rules derive from `docs/RULEBOOK.md`; map coverage in `docs/RULE_CONTRACT_TEST_INVENTORY.md`.
- Never treat full-suite green as proof a rule is enforced without a targeted test.
- See `.cursor/rules/rules-contract-testing.mdc` for contract-test workflow.
- Prefer small, focused files over large monolithic scripts.
- Do not invent extra game systems unless asked.
- Do not build the full game in one pass.

## Terminology (mandatory)

- **Macro contact resolution** — instant deterministic board resolution when macro pieces share a node (hero removes all demons). **Not** tactical combat.
- **Tactical combat** — `SpellCombatSession`; canonical spell duel for isolated sim, replay, telemetry, and future 3D human encounters. **Not in the macro economy loop.**
- **Legacy card duel** — `CombatResolver`; debug/reference unless revived.
- **Hero** — generic macro piece commanded by a god; not an RPG character.
- **3D human encounter** — future embodied layer; may pause game and lead to tactical combat; not implemented in macro loop.

See `docs/RULEBOOK.md` for full intended v1 rules.

## Game concept

This is a competitive civilisation-building board game on a hex map.

It combines:

- Settlers of Catan-style city-adjacent resource production.
- Pandemic-style heroes moving around the board to contain a spreading demonic underworld.
- Seven Wonders-style drafting of development cards, which are built into cities as special buildings.

## Current project state (2026-06)

The headless milestone is **complete and extended**. The active Godot project is `godot_game/`.

**Implemented in core (test-covered):**

- Seeded radius-3 hex board, players, cities, production
- Roads, heroes, infection-deck demon spread, macro contact resolution, breach loss (10), victory-point win
- Hero action budgets, city demon occupation, offer/accept trade, drafting skeleton, `TurnPhase`
- Legal actions, bots, event log, deterministic simulation
- Development build stub, headless card combat contract (**legacy**), `SpellCombatSession` tactical combat (isolated)
- `BotGameSession`, CSV export, reporting helpers

**Implemented in presentation (read-only / bot-advance / isolated tactical):**

- Headless CSV bot run mode
- 2D strategic playable/debug modes (near-term dev default)
- 3D wizard-world board visualisation (long-term product direction; read-only)
- Spell combat replay/play modes (isolated tactical combat)
- Legacy debug event-log overlay

**Not yet implemented:**

- M22 hex click-to-build (keyboard 2D play mode exists)
- Full drafting human pick + development-card library balance
- Dataset v2 / production RL export
- 3D human encounters and embodied wizard/combat in macro loop
- Dataset v2 / production RL export

See `docs/RULEBOOK.md`, `docs/RULES_ENGINE_AUDIT.md`, `docs/PROJECT_STATUS.md`, and `docs/NEXT_MILESTONES.md` for handoff details.

## Do not build yet

Do not build these until specifically requested:

- Drafting (full Seven Wonders-style system)
- Full development-card library beyond the current stub
- Neural network training in Godot (export telemetry only; dataset v2 before serious RL)
- Ports or Catan-style fixed trade ratios
- Integrating `SpellCombatSession` into the macro economy loop
- Finished art, animation, and polish
- Multiplayer networking
- A second parallel GameState or donor-project merge